---
source: tests/cli_input.rs
expression: long
---
Terminal-agnostic single-keystroke hint picker for scrollback.

Patterns are matched on logical rows, so a match that soft-wraps at the grid's right edge is still found whole. That needs a source that pipes logical lines: "tmux capture-pane -J", or felis' pipe action. A physical-row source ("tmux capture-pane -p", or a "cat" of already-wrapped output) has replaced the wrap with a newline before pouncer sees it, and a match split across that newline cannot be recovered.

The repaint carries the source's colors when the producer kept them: "tmux capture-pane -e", "kitty @ get-text --ansi", "--color=always" on a plain pipe, felis' pipe action with "ansi". A producer that strips SGR yields a plain repaint; nothing is guessed back.

Usage: pouncer [OPTIONS] [FILE]

Arguments:
  [FILE]
          Scrollback to scan: a path, or "-"/omitted to read stdin.
          
          A file is how a producer that runs pouncer inside an interactive terminal hands over the region, since there stdin is the keyboard (felis' pipe action).

Options:
  -e, --regex <RE>
          Regex pattern to match (repeatable).
          
          Rust regex syntax: no lookaround or backreferences. Nothing matches without --regex or --preset.

      --preset <NAME>
          Curated pattern(s): url, email, ipv4, ipv6, path, sha, uuid, filepos, hostport, hex, mdlink, jwt, pod, number.
          
          Comma-separated and repeatable; off unless listed. Where two start on the same cell, a --regex beats any preset, and among presets the one named first wins: "filepos,path" keeps "src/main.rs:12" whole.

      --capture <N>
          Pick capture group N instead of the whole match.
          
          The label still covers the whole match. Every pattern must have group N.

      --min-len <N>
          Drop matches narrower than N display columns.
          
          Measured on the whole match (across a soft wrap), not on the --capture value. Keeps a permissive pattern usable: "--preset sha" on a hex dump.
          
          [default: 0]

      --alphabet <ALPHABET>
          Characters labels are drawn from.
          
          Earlier characters make the shorter labels. Labels are at most two keys, so N characters label at most N×N matches.
          
          [default: asdfghjklqwertyuiopzxcvbnm]

      --reverse
          Give the shortest labels to the last matches

      --unique
          Share one label across identical match values

  -m, --multi
          Pick several matches: a label toggles selection, Enter confirms the set

      --action <ACTION>
          copy | open | <command with {}>. Absent prints the pick to stdout.
          
          "copy" sets the clipboard with OSC 52. "open" runs xdg-open (open on macOS, the default handler on Windows). Anything else is a command where {} stands for the picked value(s) as separate arguments: a shell command run with sh -c on Unix, and on Windows a program and its arguments, split like a C program's command line and run without a shell. All picks go to one run. Without --action each value is printed on its own line.

      --upper-action <ACTION>
          Action for a label typed in uppercase, in the same form as --action.
          
          One binding then offers two actions. Single-pick only; rejected with --multi.

      --cols <N>
          Grid width in columns for parsing and label placement.
          
          Defaults to the terminal width; set it when pouncer's terminal is not the source's width (a tmux popup narrower than the captured pane) so soft-wrap reconstructs as it did at the source. Columns past pouncer's own right edge are not drawn, and a match starting there gets no label.

      --hint-fg <COLOR>
          Hint label foreground. Default black.
          
          A color is a name (red, dark_blue, ...), an ANSI index 0-255, or #rrggbb.

      --hint-bg <COLOR>
          Hint label background, as --hint-fg. Default green

      --select-fg <COLOR>
          Selected-label foreground in --multi, as --hint-fg. Default white

      --select-bg <COLOR>
          Selected-label background in --multi, as --hint-fg. Default blue

      --dim
          Dim the repainted text so labels stand out more.
          
          Composes with the source style: a bold red cell stays bold red, dimmed.

      --generate <KIND>
          Print the man page or a shell completion script to stdout and exit

          Possible values:
          - man:           pouncer(1) in roff
          - complete-bash: bash completion script
          - complete-zsh:  zsh completion script
          - complete-fish: fish completion script

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Keys:
  a label        pick it (with --multi: toggle it)
  Shift+label    pick it for --upper-action
  Enter          confirm the --multi selection
  Backspace      undo the last typed key
  Esc, Ctrl-c, Ctrl-g
                 cancel
  arrows, PgUp/PgDn, Home/End, Ctrl-d/u/f/b
                 scroll

A single match is picked without showing the overlay.

Exit status:
  0    a match was picked and its action succeeded
  1    no matches, or an error (including a failed action)
  2    invalid command line
  130  cancelled
